Reason:
After the conversion, the code now explicitly ensures the label is NUL-terminated. If the conversion fails (`err < 0`), it sets the first byte to 0. If the conversion fills or exceeds the buffer (`err >= sizeof(sbi->volume.label)`), it forces termination at the last byte. Otherwise, it places a NUL at the position indicated by the returned byte count. This guarantees the label is always a valid C string, preventing buffer over-read.

